   "daf": "42a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "וְכֵן שְׁאָר כׇּל הַנָּשִׁים. בִּשְׁלָמָא יְבָמָה, כְּדַאֲמַרַן. אֶלָּא שְׁאָר כׇּל הַנָּשִׁים אַמַּאי?",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: «And similarly, all other women may» not be betrothed or marry until they have waited three months. The Gemara asks: «Granted, a yevama» has to wait, «in accordance with» the reason «that we said,» that if she is pregnant with viable offspring, consummating the levirate marriage would violate the prohibition against engaging in relations with one’s brother’s wife. «But» with regard to «all other women, why» shouldn’t they remarry immediately even if they are pregnant?"
  }
